From 9ee862b56f78f10178cda0b4dc91deea837b3036 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:27:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] daemon: Discover platform passkey providers

The API already lists `internal` as a transport and talks about passkey
providers, but there is no way for a provider to register with
credentialsd.

Providers now register with a drop-in file, `<id>.conf`, in
/etc/credentialsd/providers, /usr/local/share/credentialsd/providers or
/usr/share/credentialsd/providers. The file names the provider's D-Bus
name, object path and, optionally, its interface and executable. The
first file for an ID wins, so an administrator can override or mask
(with an empty file) a packaged provider from /etc. Debug builds also
read the directories in CREDSD_PROVIDER_DIRS.

credentialsd calls providers over its own gateway connection, so a
provider can check that the caller owns credentialsd's bus name. When
the drop-in names an executable, credentialsd checks that the owner of
the provider's bus name runs it before sending anything.

Every provider that answers GetInfo() within two seconds is offered as a
device with transport `internal`, unless the request asks for a
cross-platform authenticator. A locked provider is still listed.
